To allow for comparison between models, the bursts are synchronized and the ranges of mRNA and protein in the four trajectories are identical (average $\langle M_i \rangle \approx 12$ copies/cell and $\langle P_i \rangle \approx 78$ copies/cell). Note that protein copy numbers are often much larger ($ P_i \sim 10^4$~\cite{Schwanhausser2011} or $10^5$~\cite{Albayrak2016}) so that discrete trajectories become indistinguishable from their continuous counterparts.}
