		\end{align}
		stands for the representative agent's consumption propensity, i.e., her percentage of wealth consumed, in the equilibrium.
	\end{Theorem}

	Theorem \ref{thm:main} establishes the existence and uniqueness of the market equilibrium and characterizes the asset price-endowment ratios by the ODEs \eqref{eq:ODEPriceEndwomentRatio} and \eqref{eq:ODEPriceEndwomentRatioHC}. The existence and uniqueness of classical solutions to these ODEs are nontrivial to prove because $\sigma_\omega(\omega)$ degenerates to zero when $\omega$ goes to 0 and 1 and thus these two ODEs are not uniformly elliptic. One of our methodological contributions is to prove the existence and uniqueness of the solutions to these ODEs; see Appendix \ref{appx:ODE}.


