The above set is a compact subset of $\mathbb R$ on the usual topology and hence it has a maximum. Thus, define $x_1$ to be that maximum. By construction, it holds that
 \[ g(x_{1})-g(x_{0}^+)\leq \delta. \]
 Moreover, either $x_{1} = b$ or it also holds that
 \[
 g(x_{1}^+)-g(x_{0}^+)\geq \delta.
 \]
We will construct the partition inductively. Suppose the points $x_k$ have been defined up to an index $i$ in such a way that
 \[
 g(x_{k+1})-g(x_{k}^+)\leq \delta \text{ and } g(x_{k+1}^+)-g(x_{k}^+)\geq \delta,
 \]
