 \[
 g(x_{i+1}^+)-g(x_{0}^+) = \sum_{k=0}^{i} g(x_{k+1}^+)-g(x_{k}^+)\geq (i+1)\delta,
 \]
 which implies that $\mu_g([x_0,x_{i+1}])\geq (i+1)\delta$. Therefore, we necessarily reach $x_m=b$ in a finite number of steps. \qedhere

