After we truncate the hydrodynamics, \tool{} flags a number of operations in the reconstruction algorithm. This can be interpreted in two ways. Either, (a) the reconstruction algorithm does not respond well to truncation and should therefore be run at full precision, or (b) another part of the code is responsible for introducing small \fp{} errors that only
get flagged when they are amplified in the reconstruction algorithm, for example due to multiplication or cancellation. If we exclude reconstruction from 
