\paragraph*{{\bf Faithfulness}}
assesses whether the response is grounded in the retrieved passages. This metric revisits the metric provided by the Ragas system \citep{es2024ragas}. 
Specifically, given a question $q$, a generated answer $a$, and the set of retrieved documents $R$, we extract the claims appearing in the answer $a$, and assess whether each claim is entailed by at least one passage $r \in R$. Accordingly, the Faithfulness score is:

\begin{equation}
F(a, R) = \sum_{c \in C_a}\frac{NLI(c, R)}{|C_a|}\ ,
\end{equation}
where $C_a$ is the set of claims appearing in answer $a$, and $NLI(c,R)=\max_{r\in R} NLI(c,r)$.

% The Faithfulness score is graded on a continuous scale with the following representative points:
