To summarize the trends we observe, a singular detection of a GW190425-like BBH event when the predicted BBH merger rates are high results in a stringent limit on $\sigma_\chi$ over the range of $m_\chi$ considered here.
Since the $t_c$ inferred from this method is restricted by the age of the universe, the inferred upper limits on the interaction cross-section can only be explored down to $\sigma_\chi(t_{\rm Hubble}, \rho_\chi, m_\chi)$.
Given this restriction, we find that in either case, we derive the most information about DM properties from a single GW observation with the next generation of detectors, CE4020ET.

