\section{2nd-order boundary-layer fields}
\seclab{BC2ndOrderAppendix}

In this Appendix, we compute the 2nd-order, time-averaged, boundary-layer fields pressure $\pd_2$ and velocity $\vvvd_2$ in the fluid, based on the 1st- and 2nd-order expressions given in \secsref{fl_first_order}{fl_second_order}. Following \eqref{v2dSplit}, the velocity field is split in two components, $\vvvds_2 = \vvvddp + \vvvddv$, that are treated independently.

\subsection{Computation of $\textbf{\emph p}_2^{\delta}$}
\seclab{p2Appendix}

To obtain the coordinate-separated form of the source term $\grad \pd_2$ in \eqref{Laplvd2Final}, we first take the divergence of \eqref{Laplvd2}, neglect the $\div\vvvd_2$-terms of order $\Gamma$, and finally use $\Lapl \pd_2 \approx \ppsqr_\zs \pd_2$, to arrive at
%
 \beq{p2d_laplace} %eq31
 \ppsqr_\zs \pd_2 = -\rhoO \div \big[\div \avr{\vvvd_1 \vvvd_1+ \vvvl_1 \vvvd_1+ \vvvd_1 \vvvl_1} \big].
 \eeq
%
Then the coordinate-separated form of this expression is obtained by using \eqsref{double_div_AB}{vd1vl1BL}, and we arrive at the following 20-term expression for $\ppperpsqr p_2^\delta$,
%
 \bal
 \eqlab{lapl_zeta_p2d} %eq35
 &\ppperpsqr p_2^\delta=  -\rhoO\Big\{
 \\ \nn
 &
 +\pardiv\big[\pardiv \timeav{\intnab 0qq \vvvdspar}{\vvvdspar}\big] %1st term
 +\timeav{\intnab {-2}qq \vdsperp}{\vdsCperp}  %4th term
 \\ \nn
 &
 +\pardiv \big[\timeav{\intnab {-1}qq \vvvdspar}{\vdsperp} %2nd term
 %		
 +\timeav{\intnab {-1}qq \vdsperp}{\vvvdspar}\big] %3rd term
 \\ \nn
 &
 +\pardiv \big[\pardiv \timeav{\intnab 01q \vvvlspar}{\vvvdspar} \big]  %5th term
 %
 +\intnab {-2}1q  \big(\vlsperp \vdsperp \big) %8th term
 \\ \nn
 &
 +\pardiv \big[\timeav{\intnab {-1}1q \vvvlspar}{\vdsperp} %6th term
 %		
 +\timeav{\intnab {-1}1q \vlsperp}{\vvvdspar}\big] %7th term
 \\ \nn
 &
 %		
 +\pardiv\big[\pardiv \timeav{\intnab 0{\zs}q \ppperp\vvvlspar}{\vvvdspar}\big] %9th term
 %
 +\timeav{\intnab  {-2}{\zs}q \ppperp \vlsperp}{\vdsperp} %12th term
 \\ \nn
 &
 +\pardiv\big[\timeav{\intnab {-1}{\zs}q \ppperp\vvvlspar}{\vdsperp} %10th term
