\begin{abstract}
For two-parameter families of dissipative twist maps, we study the dynamics of invariant graphs and the  thresholds of their existence and breakdown. We obtain:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item For arbitrary $C^1$-small perturbations, invariant graphs with prescribed rotation numbers can be realized through parameter adjustments;

    \item The existence of almost sharp perturbations that trigger complete destruction of all invariant graphs;

    \item When the perturbation lacks $C^1$-regularity, Lipschitz invariant graphs with non-differentiable points may persist despite the Lipschitz semi-norm satisfying the requirement of the normally hyperbolic invariant manifold theorem.
\end{enumerate}
\end{abstract}



