The CBC parameters and their priors are listed in Table~\ref{tab:CBCPrior}, here we briefly describe some parameters of interest that feature in the following figures. 
The total mass, $M$, is the sum of the component masses of the compact binary in the detector frame. 
The spin angular momentum of the compact binary system can be summarized with ``effective" parameters: the effective precessing parameter $\chip$ (Eq.~(3.4) in~\cite{chi_p}) and the effective spin-aligned parameter $\chieff$ (Eq.~(2) in~\cite{LIGOScientific:2020ibl}). 
Both parameters have been shown to be susceptible to biases due to the presence of glitches in real data~\cite{Payne:2022spz, Udall:2024ovp_191109}. 

