	\begin{abstract}
 Rotary maps (orientably regular maps) are highly symmetric graph embeddings on orientable surfaces. This paper classifies all rotary maps whose underlying graphs are Praeger-Xu graphs, denoted $\operatorname{C}(p,r,s)$, 
 for any odd prime $p$ that does not divide $r$. 
 Our main result establishes a one-to-one correspondence between the isomorphism classes of these maps and the multiplicity-free representations of the dihedral group $\D_{2r}$
  over the finite field $\mathbb{F}_p$. This work extends a recent classification for the case where $p=2$.


		% \textit{MSC2010:} 05C25, 20B05, 20C15
