 % % $\operatorname{C}(p,r,s)$, 
 % and the multiplicity-free representations of the dihedral group $D_{2r}$ 
 %  over $\mathbb{F}_p$. This result allows us to classify all such maps for any odd prime $p$ not dividing $r$, extending a recent classification for $p=2$. Rotary maps (orientably regular maps) are a key class of highly symmetric graph embeddings on orientable surfaces, and our work provides a complete classification for this important family of maps with Praeger-Xu underlying graphs.
% This correspondence requires the representation's degree to be $s+1$ and excludes a specific degree-1 representation when r is even. 
	\end{abstract}
