In summary, the proposed methodology can fit a compact and low-cost design taking advantage of the robust and simple-to-operate modern atomic magnetometers. Thus, such prospecting equipment could be readily mounted on a small lunar rover. One could imagine several exploratory prospecting campaigns performed by such a rover, which in short time could survey an area for the highest abundance of $^3{\rm He}$, before the actual mining equipment takes over.

